!!! Owed rows
* RULINGS (operator 2026-11-08, quote license): 'Aprpove the hearth/ rename/tree restructure.'; 'The resolvers fall back to XDG homes when LAR_ROOT is unset. This reads design time crud from when the lararium sat in the main WSL instance, but we've gone to containerized.'; R1 AI memory never rides git by default (promotion into a git-tracked bag stays a deliberate per-memory act); R2 temp: housekeeping only, age-expiry opt-in; R3 reset with unprojected content: itemized list + typed accept-loss. Drafts stay projected (2026-11-04: 'unsaved drafts survive in CRDT state and file projection'). Road row fa5f50e16 defers identity continuity, face bundles, CRDT history, emergency restore until after M8.
* CONTROLLER RULING (2026-11-08, under the operator's 'Pick the most pono path'): the ACQUIRED LIBRARY takes its own surviving root, &lt;root>/library/. It holds originals the house acquired, not renders of the CRDT, so it sits neither in projections/ (renders) nor in hearth/ (wiped). Step 3 binds it into the container as a third mount (&lt;house>/library -> /lar/library); reset never touches it. The layout reads: hearth/ (wiped), projections/, library/, config/, cache/, run/.
* THE AIM: ONE named house root. A re-found clears &lt;root>/hearth/ alone; every deliberate plaintext projection survives in &lt;root>/projections/. Layout: &lt;root>/hearth/{vessel,identity,nexus,checkpoints,staging,sensoriums}, &lt;root>/projections/{bags,wikis,trash,audit}, &lt;root>/config/, &lt;root>/cache/, &lt;root>/run/. One level per meaning; retire the nested XDG facets (data/lares vs data/lararium, state/, vessel/st repetition) inside the root.
* STEP 1 (resolvers): packages/lararium-node/src/vessel-paths.ts and packages/lararium-mempalace/src/xdg-base.ts read LAR_ROOT ALONE; unset refuses by name (no XDG fallback, no homedir default); the table maps the layout above. The Python mirror in packages/lararium-sensorium/scripts (sensorium.py, meta_io.py, lares_uds.py, guest_harvest.py, structurepalace_io.py, bed_manifest.py, conftest.py; list EVERY resolver call site before editing: grep XDG_, homedir, expanduser, .local/share) moves in the SAME step. A weld test reads both tables and asserts them equal. ~45 tests that isolate through XDG_* switch to a scratch LAR_ROOT. Red first: unset LAR_ROOT refuses in TS and Python; the weld test. The mempalace/ submodule stays out of scope (external). Run every affected test file, not samples.
* STEP 2 (projections): packages/lararium-node/src/bag-paths.ts projectionRoots, both kahua-&lt;F> mirror factories (daemon working wiki, kahua stage) and the per-wiki grants in open-node-vessel.ts (~4036-4075) take &lt;root>/projections/. KEEP: canon-sourced bags write back to the canon source (LAR_BAGS / the checkout) with wikis beside it; bags/daemon stays unmirrored (control plane); draft recovery grants; .kapae shadows. disk-projector.ts atomicWrite: fsync the temp file, rename, fsync the parent dir, create the temp with mode 0600; name the body/.meta order so a crash never leaves new meta over an old body. Red first in packages/lararium-node/tests/projection-roots-split.test.ts: distinct state, canon and projection roots -> house bags + both kahua-&lt;F> mirrors under projections, canon in the checkout, bags/daemon absent; a test that the fsync runs.
* STEP 2 ADDS (hidden-row read, 2026-11-08, gap CONFIRMED): the working mirror follows the RESOLVED view (island-adaptor.ts:536 _landOne; disk-projector.ts:717 reconcile returns when the winner's origin bag is unmirrored; start scans wiki.allTitles() ~529, and listVisible() only for recovery mirrors ~513). A working row shadowed by a same-title draft or personal row never projects, and a crash between its sealed write and the notification leaves it off disk for good. Cure in disk-projector.ts: at start, enumerate each ordinary mirror's OWN bag records and project them through a renderer that takes the record's fields, not the resolved view; reconcile projects the mirrored bag's own record when a higher layer shadows it. Red: working + higher draft at one title, stop after the working store write before the notification, fresh projector -> the working carrier holds the working record. Control: no shadow -> the resolved working row projects as today.
* STEP 3 (container): docker-compose.surface.yml sets LAR_ROOT=/lar and binds two host dirs: &lt;house>/hearth -> /lar/hearth and &lt;house>/projections -> /lar/projections (env file names them; ~/.lares/lares-surface.env holds LARES_STATE today: rename to the house root's hearth path, and add the projections path; keep every existing refusal in the compose header about locations). tools/lares-container.sh: found passes &#45;-root /lar; reset clears &lt;house>/hearth alone (keeps the typed re-found, TTY, running-vessel and bind-holder refusals) and refuses when hearth and projections overlap or either sits inside the other or the workspace. Red first in tools/lares-container.test.mjs: reset leaves projections/ and config/; overlap refuses. Update tools/harbor-walk-witness.sh / rite-commands-witness.sh where they read the old paths. SECURITY-CLASS: the shim + compose need the controller's SHIP; say so in the hand-back.
* LAWS: evergreen prose (no history words); L-Prime in prose you write; no credential via flag/env/pipe; no new swarm-control env var (LAR_ROOT and the compose LARES_* names stand); never pnpm install outside the broker; daemon packages (node, keyhive) run single test files under the broker's test door; e2e stays in CI.
* CLAUDE.md's 'Claude Adapter Surface' section describes the projection rule and LAR_ROOT; true it in step 3 to the new tree (the controller reviews it).

